Z||000000||Rare87GT||10-29-2001||04:04 PM||||Hey guys, after reading and always checking in on the posts I finally have a reason to post because I just recently purchased a 1987 GT.  Im friends with pontiacs4me or (fieroX).  He is the one that found the car and helped me buy it.  I bought the car last Wednesday evening at 6:30pm at a small dealership for $1500.  After driving it for a hour or so we figured out that the car is Canadian, therefore all the stuff in the car is in metric.  The car also has only about 77,000 miles.  Oh and I forgot to mention the first day after I bought it, the clutch decided to go out and my friends pretty much did everything to fix it, which I am thankful for.  I drove it up to Manhattan this weekend and the car drives like a dream, very quick off the line, even got my friend in a 86 Mustang GT that runs mid 13's through the intersection.  The car is in perfect condition, just little miscellaneous parts here and there and a new paint job hopefully by summer and the car will be awesome.  Well this post is getting long so I will stop typing and listen to your guys replys.  Later.  <P>------------------<BR>1987 GT||||reg||1
